From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:23:58 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] vb-carts

Virtual Boy carts are drawn as one Virtual Boy cart in the retro bitmap
renderer (ADR 0054), the same for every region: ConsoleMods' Dimensions
for Game Cartridges gives 75.8 mm wide, 68.36 mm tall and 73.74 mm with
the dust cap, and says the NTSC-U and NTSC-J carts are identical. So
the cart is seated at 240x234 (360x351 drawn), nearly square, with
rounded top corners, a large label well over the upper two thirds, a
line across the body above the dust cap and the dust cap as a darker
band along the bottom. The plastic is grey, the SNES grey 0x9f 0x9c
0xa2; a shell colour chosen in Config/cart_shell.txt still wins.

The outline and relief are ours (vb_cart.svg, vb_cart_detail.svg), lit
into vb_neutral.png by examples/retro_neutrals.rs; every other neutral
regenerates byte for byte.
---
 crates/slot-ui/assets/retro/vb_neutral.png | Bin 0 -> 186038 bytes
 crates/slot-ui/assets/vb_cart.svg          |   3 +
 crates/slot-ui/assets/vb_cart_detail.svg   |  15 +++
 crates/slot-ui/examples/retro_neutrals.rs  |   4 +-
 crates/slot-ui/src/cart.rs                 |   6 +-
 crates/slot-ui/src/lib.rs                  |   2 +-
 crates/slot-ui/src/retro_cart.rs           |  19 +++-
 crates/slot-ui/src/retro_face.rs           |   4 +-
 crates/slot-ui/src/retro_shell.rs          |   3 +
 crates/slot-ui/tests/render_nes_shelves.rs |   5 +-
 crates/slot-ui/tests/retro_bitmap.rs       |   5 +-
 crates/slot-ui/tests/vb_cart.rs            | 119 +++++++++++++++++++++
 12 files changed, 173 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 crates/slot-ui/assets/retro/vb_neutral.png
 create mode 100644 crates/slot-ui/assets/vb_cart.svg
 create mode 100644 crates/slot-ui/assets/vb_cart_detail.svg
 create mode 100644 crates/slot-ui/tests/vb_cart.rs

diff --git a/crates/slot-ui/assets/retro/vb_neutral.png b/crates/slot-ui/assets/retro/vb_neutral.png
new file mode 100644
